From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:06:25 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] SWGL GPU path: empty samplers, CPU draws placed by the GPU,
 dual depth clears

- A sampler with nothing bound reads (0, 0, 0, 1) from a 1x1 texture,
  as in GL, instead of sending the draw to the CPU. The GPU variants of
  text and split composites have a clip mask sampler that WebRender
  leaves empty when there is no mask. That had sent all their draws to the
  CPU, onto targets whose depth only the GPU has.
- A draw that must stay on the CPU (no GPU variant: YUV, SVG filters) into
  a target that lives on the GPU is now shaded by SWGL into a scratch
  texture, without blending or depth. The GPU then places those quads on
  the real target with the draw's own blend and depth test, reading the
  scratch texture (a small copy shader; perspective-correct through
  u*w, v*w, w). No readback of the target, and depth stays where it is.
  draw_quad reports the quads it rasterizes for this.
- Depth clears happen on both the CPU and the GPU, and neither copy
  counts as newer afterwards, so draws that stay on the CPU test against
  a cleared buffer too.
- Trace lines name why a draw stays on the CPU.

On the PC these fix blend/large, the filter-mix-blend-mode crash,
text/ahem, text/raster_root_*, split/ordering, image/yuv(-clip) and
backdrop-filter-isolation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
